meta {
  name: 4 Update provider
  type: http
  seq: 5
}
put {
  url: {{providerUrl}}/api/v1/providers/{{providerEmail}}
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "firstName": "Grace",
    "lastName": "Hopper-Updated",
    "email": "{{providerEmail}}"
  }
}
docs {
  Ownership-guarded, and one of the six routes that still catches `ForbiddenException` locally. Its `403`
  body is identical to the central handler's — `app.UseStatusCodePages()` normalises both to
  ProblemDetails `{type, title, status, traceId, requestId}`.

  ⚠️ Validation runs **before** the ownership check, so an invalid body gives `400` and never reaches the
  guard. If you are testing authorization, send a valid body.
}
